{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1370386-clarification-needed-spilled-blood","id":1370386,"title":"Clarification needed(Spilled Blood)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-02-25T09:54:35-08:00","id":1370386,"title":"Clarification needed(Spilled Blood)","content":"Just some confusing wording here and there:<br /> 1) Tiny Guardian devotion, p32:<br /> &quot;As the guardians are still part of the Nosoi, if they are destroyed, she takes 1 lethal damage. Lastly, the guardians must return by sunrise; she takes 1 lethal damage for each guardian she hasn\u2019t drawn back into herself by night\u2019s end.&quot;<br /> It doesn't state clearly that the guardian dies if not absorbed before sunrise. Desceiption implies that the creature can get far from its &quot;parent&quot;(getting on the plane). Is it possible to take the damage while keeping the creature detached during the day?<br /> 2) Terra Figulina, p94:<br /> &quot;At sunrise, the [homunculus animated by this power] transforms back into raw clay. This ability lasts a week per donor Blood Potency.&quot; <br /> Ugh, what? How can it fall apart at sunrise yet last for weeks? <br /> 3) The Chimera Virus symptoms description, p126:<br /> &quot;The host vampire\u2019s gray matter is also replaced by the Chimera\u2019s mutagenic cells. It happens so gradually that the vampire is unaware of any change as the virus builds a facsimile of her neurons. Her identity and memories are intact, and her behaviors remain the same, at least at first.&quot;<br /> Well, you are not you anymore. Or you still are? The question is, do the infected have their own soul(even though they're a viral colony)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25974-goshmuz","name":"Goshmuz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-25T11:03:49-08:00","id":1370403,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25974-goshmuz\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25974\" data-vbnamecard=\"25974\">Goshmuz</a><br /> <br /> I'm just making an educated guess here, so don't pin me on this, but:<br /> <br /> 1) You probably can't keep the guardians past sunrise. If they haven't returned when the sun comes up, they'll die, thus giving you 1 lethal damage.<br /> <br /> 2) The fact that the homunculus transforms into raw clay during the day doesn't mean it dies. The sun comes up, the homunculus becomes inanimate. The sun goes down, the homunculus becomes animate again. That's how I interpret it.<br /> <br /> 3) Probably not. Does it really matter though? The way I see it, the virus takes over and changes the host, but as it does, it also becomes more like the host. The virus acts like you, but it is not you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25286-tomorrow-s-nobody","name":"Tomorrow's Nobody","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25286_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-25T11:09:57-08:00","id":1370404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Goshmuz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1370386-clarification-needed-spilled-blood#post1370386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just some confusing wording here and there:<br /> 1) Tiny Guardian devotion, p32:<br /> &quot;As the guardians are still part of the Nosoi, if they are destroyed, she takes 1 lethal damage. Lastly, the guardians must return by sunrise; she takes 1 lethal damage for each guardian she hasn\u2019t drawn back into herself by night\u2019s end.&quot;<br /> It doesn't state clearly that the guardian dies if not absorbed before sunrise. Desceiption implies that the creature can get far from its &quot;parent&quot;(getting on the plane). Is it possible to take the damage while keeping the creature detached during the day?<br /> 2) Terra Figulina, p94:<br /> &quot;At sunrise, the [homunculus animated by this power] transforms back into raw clay. This ability lasts a week per donor Blood Potency.&quot;<br /> Ugh, what? How can it fall apart at sunrise yet last for weeks?<br /> 3) The Chimera Virus symptoms description, p126:<br /> &quot;The host vampire\u2019s gray matter is also replaced by the Chimera\u2019s mutagenic cells. It happens so gradually that the vampire is unaware of any change as the virus builds a facsimile of her neurons. Her identity and memories are intact, and her behaviors remain the same, at least at first.&quot;<br /> Well, you are not you anymore. Or you still are? The question is, do the infected have their own soul(even though they're a viral colony)?</div> </div> </div> </div>As to 2): the ability to spawn the homunculus lasts the duration. The clay thing goes back inside the vampire to restore her health at the end of the night, unless it's otherwise destroyed. Rules as intended, the clay just becomes clay and doesn't respawn, but it wouldn't hurt if you played it that way (though you'd have to pay for the agg in day sleep, or spend another WP to make it permanent.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 02-25-2020, 02:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-25T13:41:48-08:00","id":1370437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tomorrow's Nobody</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1370386-clarification-needed-spilled-blood?p=1370403#post1370403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span><br /> <br /> I'm just making an educated guess here, so don't pin me on this, but:<br /> <br /> 1) You probably can't keep the guardians past sunrise. If they haven't returned when the sun comes up, they'll die, thus giving you 1 lethal damage.<br /> <br /> 2) The fact that the homunculus transforms into raw clay during the day doesn't mean it dies. The sun comes up, the homunculus becomes inanimate. The sun goes down, the homunculus becomes animate again. That's how I interpret it.<br /> <br /> 3) Probably not. Does it really matter though? The way I see it, the virus takes over and changes the host, but as it does, it also becomes more like the host. The virus acts like you, but it is not you.</div> </div> </div> </div>1)Then why damage from a dead and not absorbed guardians are mentioned twice as different things?<br /> 2)Well, the only explanation I see there.<br /> 3)It matters because I'm building a Chimera NPC. He's my representative and a probable antagonist, so I need to know for sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25974-goshmuz","name":"Goshmuz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-25T14:07:03-08:00","id":1370441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Goshmuz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1370386-clarification-needed-spilled-blood?p=1370437#post1370437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1)Then why damage from a dead and not absorbed guardians are mentioned twice as different things?<br /> 2)Well, the only explanation I see there.<br /> 3)It matters because I'm building a Chimera NPC. He's my representative and a probable antagonist, so I need to know for sure.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> 1) Yeah I understand your confusion, but I'm pretty sure the guardians are destroyed when the sun comes up and they haven't returned to the vampire yet. That's how I would rule it.<br /> <br /> \u200b2) Well, it seems like I wasn't 100% correct anyway, as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar192_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"192\" data-vbnamecard=\"192\">Yossarian</a> answered your question and clarified that the homunculus nests in the vampire's body during the day and if it fails to do so, it turns to clay.<br /> <br /> 3) In that case I would rule it in whichever way you think is more fun and dramatic for your story. Personally, I think the chimera virus is capable of emulating the host, but it is not the host. It slowly takes over, and as it does, it also learns to copy the host's behavior, but the copy isn't perfect and people might start to notice odd &quot;glitches&quot; in the infected person's behavior. Without a host, the chimera virus is just a mindless virus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25286-tomorrow-s-nobody","name":"Tomorrow's Nobody","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25286_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}